      "answerEnglish": "Space technology is used for weather forecasting, communication, agriculture, disaster management, navigation and resource mapping. Satellite data can provide farmers with weather and crop information. During disasters, satellite imagery helps assess affected areas. Communication satellites can improve connectivity in remote regions. Greater research and private participation in India's space sector can strengthen scientific capabilities, technological industries and economic opportunities."
