      "answerEnglish": "Artificial intelligence can improve efficiency in healthcare, agriculture, education, industry, finance and public services. Developing AI systems for Indian languages can improve digital inclusion. However, data privacy, algorithmic bias, cybersecurity, employment impacts and technological inequality are major concerns. India needs a responsible and transparent policy framework for AI. Investment in data quality, research, computing infrastructure and human skills is also essential."
